.Nd working notes of 2026-05-19
.Sh ENTRIES
.Ss YAML buffers still rendered as prose
.Ss Symptom
YAML files opened with variable-pitch fonts and visual-line wrapping, despite the earlier change to re-fire
.Ql "prog-mode-hook"
(commits
.Ql "0928969" ,
.Ql "bb70c5c" ).
.Ss Root cause
.Ql "yaml-mode"
/
.Ql "yaml-ts-mode"
derive from
.Ql "text-mode" ,
so
.Ql "text-mode-hook"
fires before the yaml-specific hook.
In
.Ql "init-writing.el"
that hook enables
.Ql "variable-pitch-mode" ,
.Ql "visual-line-mode" ,
and
.Ql "visual-wrap-prefix-mode" ,
and
.Ql "jinx-mode"
is also attached to
.Ql "text-mode-hook"
for prose spell-check.
Running
.Ql "prog-mode-hook"
on top added the prog niceties but did not undo the prose ones, so the buffer kept its text-mode appearance.
.Ss Fix
.Ql "lisp/init-lang-data.el"
— extended
.Ql "jotain-lang-data--enable-prog-mode-features"
to disable
.Ql "variable-pitch-mode" ,
.Ql "visual-line-mode" ,
.Ql "visual-wrap-prefix-mode" ,
and
.Ql "jinx-mode"
after running
.Ql "prog-mode-hook" .
The two visual-wrap / jinx calls are guarded so the function stays safe if those packages aren't loaded yet.
